I'm considering the design. Since it's a simple multiplexer, I can use a conditional assignment or a case statement in Verilog. The conditional operator would be concise and efficient for this case. I'll use an assign statement with a ternary operator to select between a and b based on sel.

Thinking about the code structure, I'll start with the module declaration, including the ports. All ports are one bit, so I'll use logic [0:0] for each. Then, the assign statement will handle the multiplexing logic. The ternary operator (a ? b : a) will evaluate to a when sel is 0 and b when sel is 1, which matches the requirements.

